<title>UK: Toronto-Dominion sets $200 mln 10-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Toronto-Dominion sets $200 mln 10-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated bond was announced by joint lead managers Citibank International plc and Morgan Stanley &amp; Co International Ltd.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TORONTO-DOMINION BANK</p>
<p> AMT    $200 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY  * 27.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE   FIXED/FRN     ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    27.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.35	REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+37 BP</p>
<p> NOTES    * CALL AT PAR FROM 27.MAR.02, AFTER WHICH COUPON</p>
<p>		BECOMES 3-MONTH LIBOR +100 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/UK/CA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    CANADA    HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.10	SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.25 PCT FEB 2002 U.S. TREASURY NOTE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
